Kesonode is an independent fork of Konode v1.5.1. It ports upstream code and
fixes but does not carry the upstream project's store listings, sponsorship
pages, website, issue tracker, or author branding.

The wire contract is intentionally frozen so existing data stays readable:
file prefixes (konode_*, kesonode_*), the default sync folder name (Konode),
the SyncPacket format (v1.0), SHA-256 checksums, AES-256-GCM / PBKDF2
parameters, extension IDs, and OAuth configuration all remain as upstream
defined them.

